      "handwritten_answer": {
        "text": "(1) _未识别到手写答案。_\n(2) _未识别到手写答案。_\n(3). 设 $M(x_0, y_0), P(x_1, y_1), (y_1 \\neq \\pm y_0)$.\n$N(x_0, -y_0)$.\n$x_0^2+y_0^2=9, x_1^2+y_1^2=9$.\n$l_{QM}: y-y_1=\\frac{y_0-y_1}{x_0-x_1}(x-x_1)$\n$l_{QN}: y-y_1=\\frac{-y_0-y_1}{x_0-x_1}(x-x_1)$.\n分别令 $y=0$, 则 $x_K=\\frac{x_1 y_0 - x_0 y_1}{y_0 - y_1}$\n$x_T=\\frac{x_1 y_0 + x_0 y_1}{y_0 + y_1}$\n$\\therefore |OK|\\cdot|OT|=|x_K \\cdot x_T|$\n$=|\\frac{x_1^2 y_0^2 - x_0^2 y_1^2}{y_0^2 - y_1^2}|$\n$=|\\frac{(9-y_1^2)y_0^2 - (9-y_0^2)y_1^2}{y_0^2 - y_1^2}|$\n$=9$.",
